{
  "email": "tom.becker@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see if similar messages were caught"
}

{
  "user_id": 4,
  "reason": "Account shows locked with 5 failed logins; check for suspicious activity related to reported fraud email"
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, thanks for reporting this, and you handled it exactly right. Asking for a wire transfer like that is a common fraud trick. Please don't reply to it, click anything in it, or forward it to coworkers. In Outlook, use the Report Phishing button on the message so our security team gets a copy, then delete it. One more thing: your account is currently locked after several wrong password attempts this morning from the office. They look like ordinary typos, not an attack. If you're having trouble signing in, just reply here and we'll unlock it. Also, if anyone else in Finance got the same email, or if it seemed to come from a Brightline address, please tell us so we can look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "Tom reported a fraud email asking for a $5,000 wire transfer. He says he didn't act on it: no reply, no payment, nothing entered. I followed KB-008. The email isn't in his quarantine, so it was delivered. Quarantine holds two messages: Q-1004 (spam, an invoice from harborview-supplies) and Q-1005 (malware, scanner@docs-share.example, 'Scanned document 0931.zip', not releasable). Neither is the reported email, and nothing was released. Sign-in logs: 14 in the last 14 days, all from New York on corporate or his usual home network, all during his normal hours, with Duo approvals and no hosting networks. On 10/9 between 10:10 and 10:25 ET there were 5 failed passwords from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10, and the account is now locked. This looks like Tom mistyping, not an attack. He didn't ask for an unlock, so I didn't request one and offered it in my reply instead. KB-008 escalation triggers (multiple recipients, internal sender) aren't confirmed. I asked him to tell us if either applies. Finance staff are a frequent target for wire fraud, so security may want to review the reported message once it comes in through the Report Phishing button.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
